    "body": "Work paused by a maintainer decision (2026-11-25: \"Replace the whole motion kernel in one go\"). The work stays paused until the scope of #4023 is clear.\n\n**Held work:** branch `issue/3750-shared-ring-set`, head `7d58b0c1e`. There is no pull request.\n\n**Done:**\n- Commit `9c69f004a` adds the equivalence pins. Their goldens were recorded on unchanged origin/main `138a592a1`:\n  - `offset2d_rings_unchanged_by_the_shared_planner` (motion, `pass_start_levels`): the 2D Offset around the dog-bone part. It has 8 cases: Auto with and without stock, Inside, Outside, Waterline and Offset rings, Helix and Arc entry. The goldens are `crates/motion/tests/golden/offset2d_dogbone_*.cl` and include the notes.\n  - `pocket_rings_unchanged_by_the_shared_planner` and `level_rings_unchanged_by_the_shared_planner` (motion): the 2D Pocket and the 3-D level plan on the split band of #3316.\n  - `fig8_offset_rings_unchanged_by_the_shared_planner` (app, heavy lane): the 2D Offset on `fig8.step` with 5 cases. The goldens include the notes and the verifier warnings.\n  - All these pins are green on the unchanged code. I also wrote an exact f64 dump of the motion cases to a local file, to use as a bit-exact baseline.\n- Commit `7d58b0c1e` is WIP: the code move.\n  - New `ring_set.rs` holds `RingRef`, `RingSet`, `RingSet::plan` (the old `side_plan`), `ring_plan`, `level_ring_plan` and `unswept`. Its unit tests are in `ring_set_tests.rs`: a disc gives circle rings, and a square with an island gives the same rings as `waterline_passes`.\n  - `level_rings.rs` keeps only the level curves. `level_pieces` now reads `RingRef` from the `RingSet`.\n  - New `ring_entry.rs` (`RingEntry::plan`) holds the entry steps that `pocket.rs` and `pocket_avoid.rs` both had: the air room, the #3884 refusal and the #3748 advice.\n  - `ring_links.rs` is extended in place. Only its module doc changed. No second module has that name.\n  - The decision records are `docs/decisions/3743-shared-ring-planner.md` and `docs/decisions/3750-shared-ring-set.md`.\n\n**State:**\n- `camcraft-motion` builds with no warning.\n- The pins, the lib tests, the quick gate, clippy, the light lane and the heavy step were NOT run on `7d58b0c1e`. The coordinator stopped the run.\n- The next step is to run the pins on the WIP head and compare the exact dump. If one golden moves, the move changed the output.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
